From: tas0dev <156896971+tas0dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] x86/mboot: scan each assigned PCI bus once

Assigned devices are grouped by policy kind rather than PCI bus number.  A
display controller on bus zero may therefore be followed by an NVMe controller
on another bus and then an xHCI controller on bus zero.  Do not try to create a
second Linux root bus when that happens.

Signed-off-by: tas0dev <156896971+tas0dev@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
@@ -750,14 +750,16 @@ static int __init mboot_pci_publish_frontend(void)
 	unsigned int active = 0;
 	unsigned int resource_count = 0;
 	unsigned int index;
-	u8 last_bus = 0xff;
 
 	for (index = 0; index < mboot_pci_device_count; index++) {
 		struct mboot_pci_frontend *device = &mboot_pci_devices[index];
 		u8 bus = device->info.requester >> 8;
 
-		if (bus != last_bus && mboot_pci_scan_bus(bus))
+		if (mboot_pci_buses[bus])
+			continue;
+		if (mboot_pci_scan_bus(bus))
 			return -EIO;
-		last_bus = bus;
 	}
 	for (index = 0; index < mboot_pci_device_count; index++) {
 		struct mboot_pci_frontend *device = &mboot_pci_devices[index];
-- 
